From: Calculinux <noreply@calculinux.org>
Subject: [PATCH] spi: rockchip: TX DMA burst length from the device tree

The driver hands the DMA controller a quarter of the FIFO (16 words on the
RK3506) per TX burst. On the RK3506 a burst holds the low-speed peripheral
bus for its whole length, and other masters wait behind it: the PicoCalc's
M0 audio firmware, which writes a GPIO register once per output bit, was
measured waiting up to 0.38 us for the display's 16-word bursts.

"rockchip,tx-dma-burst" sets the burst length per controller, between 1
and half the FIFO (the free space a TX DMA request guarantees). Without the
property nothing changes. On the PicoCalc's display controller (&spi0) 4
keeps the panel at 48 full frames a second at 93.75 MHz while the M0's
corrected audio loop keeps pace; 1 or 2 cannot keep the FIFO full (24 and
40 frames a second) and are worse for the M0 as well. Measurements:
picocalc-drivers luckfox-lyra/docs/m0-audio.md.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Calculinux <noreply@calculinux.org>
---
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-rockchip.c
@@ -212,6 +212,7 @@
 	u32 version;
 	/*depth of the FIFO buffer */
 	u32 fifo_len;
+	u32 tx_burst;	/* words per TX DMA burst */
 	/* frequency of spiclk */
 	u32 freq;
 	/* speed of io rate */
@@ -535,7 +536,7 @@
 			.direction = DMA_MEM_TO_DEV,
 			.dst_addr = rs->dma_addr_tx,
 			.dst_addr_width = rs->n_bytes,
-			.dst_maxburst = rs->fifo_len / 4,
+			.dst_maxburst = rs->tx_burst,
 		};
 
 		dmaengine_slave_config(ctlr->dma_tx, &txconf);
@@ -1116,6 +1117,12 @@
 		ret = -EINVAL;
 		goto err_disable_sclk_in;
 	}
+	/* TX DMA requests come when half the FIFO is free: a burst of up to
+	 * that many words fits. The default, a quarter of the FIFO, unless
+	 * the device tree asks for less. */
+	rs->tx_burst = rs->fifo_len / 4;
+	if (!of_property_read_u32(pdev->dev.of_node, "rockchip,tx-dma-burst", &rs->tx_burst))
+		rs->tx_burst = clamp(rs->tx_burst, 1U, rs->fifo_len / 2);
 	quirks_cfg = device_get_match_data(&pdev->dev);
 	if (quirks_cfg)
 		rs->max_baud_div_in_cpha = quirks_cfg->max_baud_div_in_cpha;
